      "Read the Bible and pray together": 1,
      "With a parent or caregiver, read John 20:11-18. Listen for the moment when Mary recognizes Jesus and the message he gives her.": 1,
      "The final page offers a question, Bible reading, a listening action and an original prayer. A trusted adult can help children with the sad parts of the story. Prayer does not replace rest, care or treatment.": 1,
      "About this story": 1,
      "Illustrations are imaginative composites, not eyewitness reconstructions. This story uses Luke for Mary's earlier discipleship and John for the Easter encounter; the large stone is a detail from Matthew. It does not identify Mary Magdalene with Mary of Bethany or the unnamed woman who anointed Jesus. Page eight shows later Christian remembrance, not Mary alive in a later century. The final reflection is original, not historical dialogue.": 1,
