      "Frequently Asked Questions": 1,
      "Who was Mary Magdalene?": 1,
      "A disciple of Jesus who supported his ministry and witnessed his resurrection. This retelling follows Luke's account of her discipleship and John's account of the Easter encounter.": 1,
      "Who is this storybook for?": 1,
      "Children ages 6 to 12, reading or listening with family. Nine illustrated narrative pages lead to a four-part family reflection.": 1,
      "Why is she called the apostle of the apostles?": 1,
      "The title honors the resurrection message Mary brought to the disciples. It does not mean that she was one of the Twelve. The Church celebrates her feast on July 22.": 1,
      "A storybook for children. Author: Please pray for the person who made this website.": 1
